WEBVTT

00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:36.917
Smile!

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.833
It just has to be your
face, okay? Try smiling.

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:43.000
Just my face?

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.292
Right. We'll start with just the form.

00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:51.875
How is this, Master?

00:00:55.625 --> 00:00:59.000
Of course that won't work!

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.625
What are you doing?

00:01:00.625 --> 00:01:03.875
I was teaching Ikaros how to smile.

00:01:03.875 --> 00:01:05.708
How to smile?

00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:09.458
She's says she wants
to be more human.

00:01:09.458 --> 00:01:12.667
So I tell her she has to at least
be able to make herself smile.

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:16.083
A smile doesn't necessarily
have to be from the heart.

00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:18.792
Just start by imitating
the expression, and smile.

00:01:18.792 --> 00:01:22.250
Do it like you're beaming. Beam!

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.708
Grin.

00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:26.875
You can't just say you're grinning!

00:01:26.875 --> 00:01:28.750
You haven't got it at all!

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:29.667
Smiley.

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:32.250
You're just saying it! That's not a smile!

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.667
Cheese.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:42.958
<i>And I'm... supposed to</i>
<i>be here to take Alpha back.</i>

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.042
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:01:46.042 --> 00:01:48.625
<i>What could it mean?</i>

00:01:48.625 --> 00:01:52.458
<i>A bell in my heart is ringing</i>

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:57.958
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:03.792
<i>It all started way back then </i>
<i>(ringin' ringin')</i>

00:02:03.792 --> 00:02:09.458
<i>Ever since before we were born</i>
<i>(ringin' ringin')</i>

00:02:09.458 --> 00:02:14.708
<i>you were destined to appear out of nowhere,</i>

00:02:14.708 --> 00:02:17.708
<i>right before my eyes,</i>

00:02:17.708 --> 00:02:20.500
<i>I'm sure of it</i>

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:26.167
<i>My wishes and ambitions and daydreams</i>

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:31.833
<i>take me to an unknown level and knock on a door</i>

00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:38.042
<i>You give me the key and the future</i>
<i>I need to take flight (with your wings)</i>

00:02:38.042 --> 00:02:40.958
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:44.000
<i>There's no stopping it</i>

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.667
<i>It's a sign, rung by an angel, saying "I love you"</i>

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:52.542
<i>Can you hear my heart bell?</i>

00:02:52.542 --> 00:02:54.875
<i>What could it mean?</i>

00:02:54.875 --> 00:03:00.292
<i>A bell in my heart that I've </i>
<i>never heard before is ringing</i>

00:03:00.292 --> 00:03:10.125
<i>But even so, you don't suspect a thing</i>

00:03:14.708 --> 00:03:16.583
The Age of Exploration.

00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:19.625
The Europeans had
discovered the New World,

00:03:19.625 --> 00:03:23.917
and in the name of colonialism,
underwent global expansion.

00:03:23.917 --> 00:03:27.500
Japan would not remain
uninvolved, either.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:31.292
At the time, large numbers of
Japanese were sent to Europe,

00:03:31.292 --> 00:03:33.667
and treated as slaves.

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:37.042
When their leader,
Toyotomi Hideyoshi, learned of this,

00:03:37.042 --> 00:03:39.750
he banished the Jesuits from the country.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:43.708
This was the beginning of
Japan's isolationist policy.

00:03:43.708 --> 00:03:48.458
Behind the glamorous foreign
diplomacy lurked a slave trade.

00:03:48.458 --> 00:03:52.542
People's greed made
them treat their fellow men

00:03:52.542 --> 00:03:55.292
as livestock, or pack animals.

00:03:55.292 --> 00:03:59.000
Perhaps, in the New World
floating in the sky,

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.375
a new class of slaves has been created,

00:04:01.375 --> 00:04:05.417
to satisfy the greed
of their leaders, as well.

00:04:06.292 --> 00:04:09.417
"Chains of No Escape"

00:04:09.833 --> 00:04:11.958
Huh? How to smile?

00:04:11.958 --> 00:04:15.250
That's right. She can't smile,
no matter what we try.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.875
Can you think of any way?

00:04:16.875 --> 00:04:21.208
Hmm, the thing is, smiles are
something that happen spontaneously.

00:04:21.208 --> 00:04:25.167
I know! Ikaros, do a <i>banzai </i>cheer for me.

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:26.917
A <i>banzai </i>cheer?

00:04:26.917 --> 00:04:27.708
Yes!

00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:29.583
Coochie-coochie-coochie!

00:04:30.417 --> 00:04:32.583
Well? It tickles, right?

00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:35.042
Ikaros, even you
have to laugh at this--

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:38.292
What?! What's wrong?!

00:04:38.292 --> 00:04:39.833
Looks like she's ticklish.

00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:41.583
And that reaction isn't weird?

00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:43.833
No! No! No!

00:04:43.833 --> 00:04:47.833
Sohara, your tickling
method is not up to par!

00:04:47.833 --> 00:04:51.750
Allow me to demonstrate!
Coochie-coochie-coochie-coochie!

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.250
<i>This </i>is tickling!

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.458
Tomo--!

00:04:54.458 --> 00:04:57.458
--Well? How about that, huh?
--Stop it!

00:05:03.208 --> 00:05:05.375
U-Uh-oh...

00:05:06.875 --> 00:05:10.042
What do you think you're doing?!

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:12.000
I do not understand.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.625
What can I do that will make me smile?

00:05:15.625 --> 00:05:17.125
I know!

00:05:17.125 --> 00:05:18.292
What?

00:05:18.292 --> 00:05:20.583
How to smile?

00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:23.375
Could you give her some advice?

00:05:32.083 --> 00:05:35.083
Takehara sure was funny earlier, huh?

00:05:50.417 --> 00:05:53.792
I guess it was no help asking
someone who never smiles, huh?

00:05:53.792 --> 00:05:56.333
Let's go, Alpha.

00:05:56.333 --> 00:05:58.417
What should I do so that I can smile?

00:05:58.417 --> 00:06:00.000
Beats me.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.000
My... if it isn't Ikaros and Nymph.

00:06:07.583 --> 00:06:09.833
How to smile, huh?

00:06:09.833 --> 00:06:10.583
Yes.

00:06:10.583 --> 00:06:11.333
"Student Council Room"

00:06:11.333 --> 00:06:12.833
It is difficult.

00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:13.458
"World Domination"

00:06:13.458 --> 00:06:18.792
Like, say, at what times
do you smile, Chairman?

00:06:18.792 --> 00:06:20.500
Let's see...

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:24.500
When I get in a really solid
whack with a flyswatter, I'd say--

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.625
like, on a person.

00:06:42.625 --> 00:06:45.042
St-Stop!!

00:07:02.875 --> 00:07:04.375
Tomoki...?

00:07:04.375 --> 00:07:07.750
Now that's hilarious.

00:07:10.917 --> 00:07:12.417
Good grief,

00:07:12.417 --> 00:07:14.125
what am I going to do with you?

00:07:14.125 --> 00:07:15.167
I am sorry.

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:17.083
Oh, it's all right, isn't it?

00:07:17.083 --> 00:07:19.667
Your life wasn't actually in peril.

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:21.167
It is <i>not </i>all right!

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:23.667
And Chairman, please don't
tell her to do anything weird!

00:07:23.667 --> 00:07:28.042
So, have you gotten to where
you can smile at all, Alpha?

00:07:28.042 --> 00:07:31.750
Mm-mm... not yet.

00:07:32.917 --> 00:07:36.833
Hmm, come to think of it,
Christmas is almost here.

00:07:36.833 --> 00:07:37.917
I know!

00:07:37.917 --> 00:07:41.667
This coming Sunday, let's all
get together at Tomoki's place,

00:07:41.667 --> 00:07:44.375
and have a Christmas party!

00:07:44.375 --> 00:07:50.042
If we all have a merry old time together,
it might make Ikaros smile.

00:07:50.042 --> 00:07:50.875
Indeed.

00:07:50.875 --> 00:07:52.500
Sounds like fun.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.792
Come on, Tomo, let's do it.

00:07:54.792 --> 00:07:57.500
I'll have my mom bake a cake.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:01.208
We'll decorate, and exchange presents!

00:08:01.208 --> 00:08:04.875
Yeah, sure.

00:08:04.875 --> 00:08:08.042
Okay, Sunday. It's a date!

00:08:09.958 --> 00:08:13.250
Why... can I not smile?

00:08:17.708 --> 00:08:21.750
I know I removed your
emotion block a long time ago.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:24.542
You are an Angeloid specializing in combat,

00:08:24.542 --> 00:08:27.083
so maybe that's just how
your functions in that area are.

00:08:27.083 --> 00:08:30.583
I am... a combat model...

00:08:30.583 --> 00:08:33.375
Well, being able to
smile is a simple thing.

00:08:33.375 --> 00:08:35.167
You don't need to agonize over it.

00:08:35.167 --> 00:08:37.458
It is not simple.

00:08:37.458 --> 00:08:46.458
After all, I have not seen
you smile, either, Nymph.

00:08:46.458 --> 00:08:49.458
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:08:49.458 --> 00:08:52.292
I have not seen you.

00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:04.250
I...

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:09.667
...have not seen you smile, Nymph,

00:09:09.667 --> 00:09:12.750
in all this time.

00:09:14.708 --> 00:09:22.917
You're right. Perhaps we Angeloids
have never genuinely smiled.

00:09:22.917 --> 00:09:31.167
What is more, there is something
that seems to be on your mind lately.

00:09:31.167 --> 00:09:36.625
I do not know what
that might be, though.

00:09:39.875 --> 00:09:42.958
All right, then.
Let's think about it together.

00:09:42.958 --> 00:09:48.250
How can we Angeloids
manage to smile? Okay?

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.750
Mm-hmm.

00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:58.583
Ah... I'm so hungry. Hey...

00:09:58.583 --> 00:09:59.958
Ikaros...

00:09:59.958 --> 00:10:02.792
Yes, Master?

00:10:06.792 --> 00:10:10.583
Good... morning...

00:10:10.583 --> 00:10:12.333
Master.

00:10:12.333 --> 00:10:16.417
<i>Take it easy! Take it easy!</i>
<i>Remember, she has wings!</i>

00:10:16.417 --> 00:10:19.375
Is something... the matter?

00:10:19.375 --> 00:10:20.667
N-No...

00:10:20.667 --> 00:10:23.417
<i>Her rack is huge! I mean...</i>

00:10:23.417 --> 00:10:25.750
Wait, wait, wait!

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:29.500
--Just a moment, now...
--Your face is red, Master.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.792
Huh...?

00:10:30.792 --> 00:10:35.000
Hey, what have you done?

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.542
Your face is hardened like this!

00:10:37.542 --> 00:10:40.375
Is that no good? We forced her
to make that expression,

00:10:40.375 --> 00:10:42.375
then solidified it with some
fixative.

00:10:42.375 --> 00:10:44.125
Are you guys idiots?!

00:10:44.125 --> 00:10:48.083
Come on, hurry and wash your face!

00:10:49.333 --> 00:10:52.083
Tomoki, you were a little
pleased by that, weren't you?

00:10:52.083 --> 00:10:53.458
Sh-Shut up!

00:10:53.458 --> 00:10:56.417
Can't you smile when
you look at me anymore?

00:10:56.417 --> 00:10:57.875
N-No...

00:10:57.875 --> 00:11:00.208
I know. Why don't you go on a date with me?

00:11:00.208 --> 00:11:01.792
If you walk down that
tree-lined avenue with me,

00:11:01.792 --> 00:11:02.667
--you might get your smile back.

00:11:02.667 --> 00:11:05.500
--What is a date?
--you might get your smile back.

00:11:08.542 --> 00:11:10.042
Tomoki,

00:11:10.875 --> 00:11:13.500
I had a great idea.

00:11:14.167 --> 00:11:16.917
Let's all three of us go on a date.

00:11:16.917 --> 00:11:18.333
Huh?!

00:11:19.833 --> 00:11:24.167
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:29.792
You guys don't really know
what a date means, do you?

00:11:29.792 --> 00:11:34.458
Dates have always been something
that men and women pair up on.

00:11:34.458 --> 00:11:36.250
You mean you can't
do it with three people?

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.583
No, that's not what the problem is.

00:11:38.583 --> 00:11:40.125
Then it's okay, isn't it?

00:11:40.125 --> 00:11:42.917
Sohara did say that
if we did something fun,

00:11:42.917 --> 00:11:46.125
Alpha might manage a smile, right?

00:11:46.125 --> 00:11:48.583
Besides...

00:11:48.583 --> 00:11:51.042
...I'm sure we'll look back fondly on this.

00:11:51.042 --> 00:11:58.042
<i>A date with Master...</i>
<i>What is this? I feel excited.</i>

00:11:58.042 --> 00:12:02.125
Ah, fine. Well then,
I'd like to start our date now.

00:12:02.125 --> 00:12:03.917
What do we do on a date?

00:12:03.917 --> 00:12:08.125
Well, on a date, we...

00:12:08.125 --> 00:12:12.333
Yeah, what do we do, anyway?

00:12:12.333 --> 00:12:14.208
<i>Sakurai Tomoki...</i>

00:12:14.208 --> 00:12:17.458
<i>...has never been</i>
<i>popular in his entire life.</i>

00:12:17.458 --> 00:12:20.917
<i>He has also never had</i>
<i>any reason to be on a date.</i>

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:22.375
"How to Date"

00:12:23.417 --> 00:12:25.667
Hey, let me see that a minute!

00:12:25.667 --> 00:12:27.792
<i>"Take your date shopping.</i>

00:12:27.792 --> 00:12:30.250
<i>If you give her something she</i>
<i>wants as a present,</i>

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.250
<i>your stock with her will rise."</i>

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.250
<i>That's it!</i>

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:37.542
All right, you guys,
go buy whatever you like!

00:12:40.292 --> 00:12:44.458
<i>Come to think of it,</i>
<i>Christmas is almost here.</i>

00:12:44.458 --> 00:12:47.375
<i>I have to think of</i>
<i>what presents I should get.</i>

00:12:47.375 --> 00:12:50.583
Master, I bought these.

00:12:50.583 --> 00:12:53.625
Did you buy the grocer out?!

00:12:53.625 --> 00:12:57.625
What's the matter, Nymph?
Isn't there anything you want to buy?

00:12:57.625 --> 00:13:02.708
I was going to buy something...
but it doesn't matter.

00:13:02.708 --> 00:13:07.833
Even if you bought it for me now,
there wouldn't be any meaning.

00:13:10.083 --> 00:13:12.875
<i>"There are many more</i>
<i>places to take your date.</i>

00:13:12.875 --> 00:13:16.458
<i>How about going to a touching movie?"</i>

00:13:17.708 --> 00:13:20.417
Were there any movies
you wanted to see?

00:13:20.417 --> 00:13:20.958
"The Pink Pantser"

00:13:20.958 --> 00:13:22.125
How about this?

00:13:22.125 --> 00:13:23.792
Absolutely not!

00:13:23.792 --> 00:13:25.292
Why not?

00:13:25.292 --> 00:13:27.125
Master, how about this?

00:13:27.125 --> 00:13:30.125
"Watermelonman"

00:13:30.125 --> 00:13:33.083
Forget about the movie.
What's next?

00:13:33.083 --> 00:13:34.833
<i>"Why not go to a theme park,</i>

00:13:34.833 --> 00:13:38.542
<i>where you can rub elbows</i>
<i>with beloved characters?"</i>

00:13:44.625 --> 00:13:47.042
Stop that!

00:13:48.042 --> 00:13:52.750
Well, we're already here.
Let's go ride some of the rides.

00:13:58.792 --> 00:14:00.333
<i>Master...</i>

00:14:00.333 --> 00:14:02.667
<i>...is delighted.</i>

00:14:03.708 --> 00:14:07.917
The whole world is spinning around me!

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:11.792
Bleh... I feel sick...

00:14:11.792 --> 00:14:13.750
Are you all right?

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:18.708
<i>A date with Master is fun...</i>

00:14:18.708 --> 00:14:20.583
<i>...but something is not right.</i>

00:14:20.583 --> 00:14:24.292
You're so pathetic.
Come on, we're going to the next place.

00:14:24.292 --> 00:14:26.875
Get up, Tomoki.

00:14:33.708 --> 00:14:36.875
Commencing system scan...
No damage to any systems...

00:14:36.875 --> 00:14:38.792
Biological structures operating normally...

00:14:38.792 --> 00:14:41.167
Reactor operating normally...

00:14:41.167 --> 00:14:42.958
All green.

00:14:42.958 --> 00:14:46.208
<i>What was that just now?</i>

00:14:46.208 --> 00:14:50.917
<i>For a moment, it seemed</i>
<i>like I felt pain in my reactor...</i>

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:00.625
Wow, amazing!

00:15:00.625 --> 00:15:03.708
<i>Well, well, she's finally settled down.</i>

00:15:03.708 --> 00:15:07.292
I'm going to go get some tea.

00:15:11.333 --> 00:15:14.042
You two take your time looking, okay?

00:15:17.875 --> 00:15:22.250
<i>I wish Tomoki had been my master.</i>

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:27.333
<i>But he's not... my master...</i>

00:15:27.333 --> 00:15:30.208
Say, Alpha...

00:15:30.208 --> 00:15:35.042
Why do you suppose
these animals are in cages?

00:15:35.042 --> 00:15:36.583
Who knows?

00:15:36.583 --> 00:15:39.667
Do you suppose these cages...

00:15:39.667 --> 00:15:43.625
...are something like our collars?

00:15:45.333 --> 00:15:49.667
If that's the case,
they'd want to run away.

00:15:49.667 --> 00:15:53.083
Isn't that right, Alpha?

00:15:53.083 --> 00:15:57.292
I'm sure that these guys would
be happier if they got out of here,

00:15:57.292 --> 00:15:59.250
and were free.

00:16:00.208 --> 00:16:05.500
If they were able to escape,
do you think Tomoki would be delighted?

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.042
Master?

00:16:07.958 --> 00:16:12.000
<i>Master... will be delighted...</i>

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.833
Say, Alpha--

00:16:17.083 --> 00:16:19.083
Whoa, Alpha!

00:16:22.833 --> 00:16:24.667
<i>Master...</i>

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.333
<i>Master...</i>

00:16:28.542 --> 00:16:30.542
<i>...will be delighted...</i>

00:16:35.125 --> 00:16:38.333
Nothing beats peace and quiet, all right.

00:16:46.875 --> 00:16:51.417
<i>It's them! This is definitely</i>
<i>Ikaros and Nymph's doing!</i>

00:16:52.208 --> 00:16:55.917
Hey! Just a minute, you!

00:16:55.917 --> 00:16:58.875
<i>Master will be delighted...</i>

00:17:03.833 --> 00:17:05.667
<i>Master...</i>

00:17:07.833 --> 00:17:09.833
<i>...will be delighted...</i>

00:17:13.208 --> 00:17:15.792
Take it easy, everyone!

00:17:15.792 --> 00:17:19.083
Please, return to your cages!

00:17:23.583 --> 00:17:25.500
What? There's a
naked man inside the park

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:28.125
running around, destroying cages?!

00:17:28.125 --> 00:17:30.667
All cars, proceed immediately to the scene!

00:17:30.667 --> 00:17:33.833
Repeat, all cars,
proceed immediately to the scene!

00:17:33.833 --> 00:17:35.917
A new terrorist group?

00:17:35.917 --> 00:17:38.083
Go to heightened alert status!

00:17:38.083 --> 00:17:39.917
Mess with us, will you?!

00:17:39.917 --> 00:17:41.333
Damn you!

00:17:41.333 --> 00:17:43.333
Take back our peace!

00:17:47.333 --> 00:17:51.333
Today, shortly after noon,
a naked man was allegedly running loose

00:17:51.333 --> 00:17:53.875
inside the zoo at a theme park.

00:17:53.875 --> 00:17:56.375
I knew he would do
something like this eventually.

00:17:56.375 --> 00:17:58.542
He's really a good person at heart.

00:17:58.542 --> 00:18:01.625
Capital punishment!
I demand capital punishment!

00:18:01.625 --> 00:18:03.917
I'm innocent!

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:10.500
I am sorry, Master.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.125
Never mind! We're going home!

00:18:13.125 --> 00:18:15.917
We've done plenty of date stuff, right?

00:18:15.917 --> 00:18:18.250
There's still something
missing, isn't there?

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:20.500
Huh? Like what?

00:18:20.583 --> 00:18:22.500
"At the end of the date, kiss him"

00:18:22.708 --> 00:18:23.875
Are you dense?!

00:18:23.875 --> 00:18:27.750
But it says here that at the
end of a date, you should kiss.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:31.708
K-Kissing is only done with the one
you have in your heart, you know!

00:18:31.708 --> 00:18:36.708
Oh... You can only do
it with one person.

00:18:37.917 --> 00:18:40.375
Say, Alpha...

00:18:40.375 --> 00:18:42.875
...I want to do it.

00:18:42.875 --> 00:18:45.292
That's okay, right, Alpha?

00:18:47.333 --> 00:18:50.417
Hey! Listen to me!

00:18:50.417 --> 00:18:52.250
Tomoki...

00:19:01.542 --> 00:19:03.542
Hey, where are you going?!

00:19:03.542 --> 00:19:06.250
D-Don't leave me here!

00:19:07.833 --> 00:19:10.792
<i>W-What should I do?</i>

00:19:14.917 --> 00:19:17.208
No, stop!

00:19:17.208 --> 00:19:20.208
Sorry! I-It was a joke! A joke!

00:19:21.125 --> 00:19:28.917
<i>W-What is this feeling?</i>
<i>What's happening? Am I...</i>

00:19:28.917 --> 00:19:31.667
<i>...getting feelings for Tomoki?</i>

00:19:32.917 --> 00:19:34.625
Hey...

00:19:34.625 --> 00:19:37.125
Are you all right?

00:19:37.458 --> 00:19:41.750
It's nothing! My reactor is
just a little out of whack!

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:43.792
Don't hit me!

00:19:43.792 --> 00:19:48.000
I've done a bad thing to Alpha.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.000
Hey, hold on!

00:19:52.625 --> 00:19:55.042
<i>I'm sorry, Alpha.</i>

00:19:55.042 --> 00:19:59.542
<i>I just wanted to have</i>
<i>one more, final memory.</i>

00:19:59.542 --> 00:20:01.875
<i>But I've had enough.</i>

00:20:01.875 --> 00:20:05.583
Reactor function 100% normal.

00:20:08.833 --> 00:20:15.458
<i>The time we spent together</i>
<i>wasn't very long, but it was fun.</i>

00:20:15.458 --> 00:20:20.375
<i>It's all right, Alpha.</i>
<i>Even if you aren't able to smile,</i>

00:20:20.375 --> 00:20:24.667
<i>with Tomoki as your master,</i>
<i>he will take good care of you,</i>

00:20:24.667 --> 00:20:26.667
<i>forever and ever.</i>

00:20:33.792 --> 00:20:36.750
My reactor...

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.375
...hurts.

00:20:46.833 --> 00:20:48.792
No sooner do you go off on your own

00:20:48.792 --> 00:20:51.208
than you come back looking all ragged.

00:20:51.208 --> 00:20:53.208
I am sorry, Master.

00:20:53.208 --> 00:20:57.208
Nymph up and leaves on me, too.
What the hell is going on?

00:20:57.208 --> 00:21:02.250
We went to all the trouble of
this date, and I still cannot smile.

00:21:08.833 --> 00:21:12.542
Come on, we're going home.
As for our date,

00:21:12.542 --> 00:21:15.500
the date is over once we get home.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.875
Yes...

00:21:28.708 --> 00:21:32.667
You've been set free. Good for you.

00:21:45.208 --> 00:21:49.208
Farewell, Alpha. Farewell, Tomoki.

00:21:59.417 --> 00:22:11.917
<i>I'll pick a red flower</i>
<i>and give it to my lover</i>

00:22:11.917 --> 00:22:24.417
<i>I'll place this flower</i>
<i>in my lover's hair</i>

00:22:24.417 --> 00:22:39.583
<i>Red flower, red flower,</i>
<i>in my lover's hair,</i>

00:22:39.583 --> 00:22:51.875
<i>you will bloom and bounce,</i>
<i>just like the sun</i>

00:22:59.917 --> 00:23:10.042
<i>Just like the moon</i>

00:23:16.875 --> 00:23:20.583
Now then, where shall I do this?

00:23:20.583 --> 00:23:25.208
The sea? Or up in the mountains,
where no one is around?

00:23:25.208 --> 00:23:30.417
If I pass away someplace
secluded, no one will notice.

00:23:30.417 --> 00:23:34.583
Then again, going back to
Synapse with a bomb in tow

00:23:34.583 --> 00:23:36.458
might be comical, too.

00:23:36.458 --> 00:23:41.167
I wonder what my
master would say if I did that.

00:24:01.708 --> 00:24:03.833
Gammas...

00:24:03.833 --> 00:24:08.086
Next time, "Queen of the Sky"
